        "original_id": "408a73cd-553e-5128-a5b5-af34a987b7ea",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Maria Callas, Vincenzo Bellini, John Ardoin\n- Roles: opera soprano, opera composer, music critic\n- Topics: opera repertoire, bel canto, opera seria\n\nFacts:\n- Vincenzo Bellini was born on 3 November 1801 and died on 23 September 1835.\n- Vincenzo Bellini was an Italian opera composer known for long-flowing melodic lines and was called \"the Swan of Catania.\"\n- John Ardoin was born on January 8, 1935 in Alexandria, Louisiana, and died on March 18, 2001 in San José, Costa Rica.\n- John Ardoin served as the music critic of The Dallas Morning News for thirty-two years.\n- John Ardoin was especially known for his friendship with Maria Callas and for his encyclopedic knowledge of her work.\n- John Ardoin wrote four books about Maria Callas.\n- Maria Callas's repertoire ranged from classical opera seria to bel canto operas by Donizetti, Bellini, and Rossini, as well as works by Verdi and Puccini.\n- In her early career, Maria Callas also performed Wagner's music dramas.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "5de00939-10c1-5944-96f1-092efd8a1f3c",
        "text": "Page: Maria Callas. Sentence: Her repertoire ranged from classical \"opera seria\" to the \"bel canto\" operas of Donizetti, Bellini and Rossini and further, to the works of Verdi and Puccini; and, in her early career, to the music dramas of Wagner.\nPage: Vincenzo Bellini. Sentence: Vincenzo Salvatore Carmelo Francesco Bellini (] ; 3 November 1801 – 23 September 1835) was an Italian opera composer, who was known for his long-flowing melodic lines for which he was named \"the Swan of Catania\".\nPage: John Ardoin. Sentence: John Ardoin, (January 8, 1935 in Alexandria, Louisiana – March 18, 2001 in San José, Costa Rica), was best known as the music critic of \"The Dallas Morning News\" for thirty-two years and especially for his friendship with and encyclopedic knowledge of the work of the famous opera soprano, Maria Callas, about whom he wrote four books.",
        "type": "DocumentChunk"
